The model is code, and the content is files. When you change the model, some changes also need a change to the files. Mica does not change the content for you. Change the model and the content in one commit: Git is the undo.

## Which changes are safe

| Change | Safe | What to do |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Add a field that is not required | Yes | Nothing. Old entries have no value. |
| Change a label, a description, `listed`, `group`, `width` or a limit | Yes | Nothing. Run `npx mica check`: a new limit can make an old value wrong. |
| Add an option to a `select()` | Yes | Nothing. |
| Remove a field | Yes | Nothing. The value stays in the file until the next save of that entry. |
| Add a required field | No | `npx mica check` reports each old entry without a value, and an editor cannot publish a change to it before it has one. Give them a value with `fill-field.mjs`, or let editors do it. |
| Rename a field | No | The editor and Astro do not see the old key, so the value seems to be lost. It is still in the file. Use `rename-field.mjs`. For a rich-text field, it renames the `.mdoc` file. |
| Change `text()` or `textarea()` to `richText()` | No | The value moves from the JSON file to a `.mdoc` file. Run `npx mica migrate-layout`, then `text-to-rich-text.mjs`. |
| Change a field to another kind | No | The old values do not validate. `npx mica check` lists them. Change them by hand, or change one of the scripts. |
| Change the `value` of a `select()` option | No | Like a rename of a value. `npx mica check` lists the entries. |
| Add the first `richText()` or `media()` field to a collection, or remove the last one | No | The entries change from files to folders, or the reverse. Run `npx mica migrate-layout`. |
| Rename a collection | No | Rename its folder with `git mv content/old content/new`, and change each `relation({ collection })` that names it. |

## The steps

1. If editors use a self-hosted Mica, publish or discard their pending changes first. A saved change has the old shape.
2. Change the model in `src/mica.ts`.
3. Run `npx astro sync`. It writes the new model to `content/.mica/schema.json` first. After a layout change or a new required field, it then stops with an error about the old entries. That is expected: the next steps fix them.
4. Run `npx mica migrate-layout` if the layout changed.
5. Run the script for your change.
6. Run `npx mica check`. It must show no errors.
7. Commit the model, `.mica/schema.json` and the content together.

## The scripts

Copy a script into your project, for example to `scripts/`, and run it with Node. Each script uses only `@micacms/core`, which your project already has. It reads the model from `.mica/schema.json`, and it finds each entry, in either layout.

The scripts change the top-level fields of the entries of one collection. For a singleton or a field in an `object()`, change the script. A script stops with a message when the collection does not exist, or when a rename would overwrite a value. Mica's CI runs each script on test content, so the scripts on this page work with the current version.

### Rename a field

```bash
node scripts/rename-field.mjs content team title role
```

```js
// Renames a top-level field in every entry of a collection, also a rich-text field and its .mdoc file.
// Change the model and run `npx astro sync` first. node rename-field.mjs <content root> <collection> <old key> <new key>
import { existsSync } from "node:fs";
import { readFile, rename, writeFile } from "node:fs/promises";
import { join } from "node:path";

import { collectionEntryPath, collectionSlugs, documentName, entryLayout, INDEX_FILE, MANIFEST_PATH } from "@micacms/core";
import { fileSystemSource } from "@micacms/core/node";

const [root, collection, from, to] = process.argv.slice(2);
const manifest = JSON.parse(await readFile(join(root, MANIFEST_PATH), "utf8"));
const def = manifest.collections[collection];
if (!def) throw new Error(`The model has no collection "${collection}".`);

for (const slug of await collectionSlugs(fileSystemSource(root), def, collection)) {
  const base = join(root, collectionEntryPath(def.fields, collection, slug));
  if (def.fields[to]?.kind === "richText") {
    // Rich text is a file beside index.json, not a key in it.
    const [old, renamed] = [join(base, documentName([from])), join(base, documentName([to]))];
    if (existsSync(renamed)) throw new Error(`${renamed} exists already.`);
    if (existsSync(old)) await rename(old, renamed);
    continue;
  }
  const file = entryLayout(def.fields) === "file" ? base : join(base, INDEX_FILE);
  const data = JSON.parse(await readFile(file, "utf8"));
  if (!(from in data)) continue;
  if (to in data) throw new Error(`${file} has "${to}" already.`);
  // The key keeps its place, so the diff shows one changed line.
  const renamed = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(data).map(([key, value]) => [key === from ? to : key, value]));
  await writeFile(file, `${JSON.stringify(renamed, null, 2)}\n`);
}
```

### Move text to rich text

```bash
npx mica migrate-layout
node scripts/text-to-rich-text.mjs content news summary
```

```js
// Moves a text value out of index.json into the field's .mdoc file, after text() became richText().
// Run `npx mica migrate-layout` first. node text-to-rich-text.mjs <content root> <collection> <key>
import { readFile, writeFile } from "node:fs/promises";
import { join } from "node:path";

import { collectionEntryPath, collectionSlugs, documentName, INDEX_FILE, MANIFEST_PATH } from "@micacms/core";
import { fileSystemSource } from "@micacms/core/node";

const [root, collection, key] = process.argv.slice(2);
const manifest = JSON.parse(await readFile(join(root, MANIFEST_PATH), "utf8"));
const def = manifest.collections[collection];
if (!def) throw new Error(`The model has no collection "${collection}".`);

// Markdoc reads these characters as markup, and a list or a rule at the start of a line; a backslash keeps them as text.
const escape = (line) =>
  line
    .replace(/[\\`*_{}[\]<>#|~]/g, "\\$&")
    .replace(/^([-+])/, "\\$1")
    .replace(/^(\d+)([.)])/, "$1\\$2");

for (const slug of await collectionSlugs(fileSystemSource(root), def, collection)) {
  const base = join(root, collectionEntryPath(def.fields, collection, slug));
  const file = join(base, INDEX_FILE);
  const data = JSON.parse(await readFile(file, "utf8"));
  const value = data[key];
  if (typeof value !== "string") continue;
  delete data[key];
  // Each line of the old text becomes a paragraph.
  const paragraphs = value.split(/\r?\n/).map((line) => escape(line.trim())).filter(Boolean);
  if (paragraphs.length > 0) await writeFile(join(base, documentName([key])), `${paragraphs.join("\n\n")}\n`);
  await writeFile(file, `${JSON.stringify(data, null, 2)}\n`);
}
```

Each line of the old text becomes a paragraph. Characters that Markdoc reads as markup, such as `*` and `#`, and a list marker or a rule at the start of a line, get a backslash, so they stay text. Look at the result in the editor.

### Give a field a value

```bash
node scripts/fill-field.mjs content team role '"Consultant"'
```

```js
// Gives a top-level field a value in every entry of a collection that has none, for example after a new required field.
// Change the model and run `npx astro sync` first. node fill-field.mjs <content root> <collection> <key> <value as JSON>
import { readFile, writeFile } from "node:fs/promises";
import { join } from "node:path";

import { collectionEntryPath, collectionSlugs, entryLayout, INDEX_FILE, MANIFEST_PATH } from "@micacms/core";
import { fileSystemSource } from "@micacms/core/node";

const [root, collection, key, json] = process.argv.slice(2);
const value = JSON.parse(json);
const manifest = JSON.parse(await readFile(join(root, MANIFEST_PATH), "utf8"));
const def = manifest.collections[collection];
if (!def) throw new Error(`The model has no collection "${collection}".`);
if (def.fields[key]?.kind === "richText") throw new Error(`"${key}" is rich text, which is a file: write it in the editor.`);

for (const slug of await collectionSlugs(fileSystemSource(root), def, collection)) {
  const base = collectionEntryPath(def.fields, collection, slug);
  const file = join(root, entryLayout(def.fields) === "file" ? base : `${base}/${INDEX_FILE}`);
  const data = JSON.parse(await readFile(file, "utf8"));
  if (data[key] !== undefined && data[key] !== null && data[key] !== "") continue;
  data[key] = value;
  await writeFile(file, `${JSON.stringify(data, null, 2)}\n`);
}
```

The value is JSON: a text in double quotes, a number, `true`, or a list. The script does not fill a rich-text field, because rich text is a file: write it in the editor.

## There is no automatic rename

Mica has no `renamedFrom` option that reads an old key. A rename with the script is one commit, and after it the files and the model agree. See [Fields](/docs/reference-fields/) and [Command line](/docs/reference-cli/).
